@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #2C3E50
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F4FD
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2C3E50
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #7F8C8D
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #EBF5FB
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FDEBD0
skinparam noteFontSize 11

title Singleton Pattern - Double-Checked Locking Sequence\n(ThreadSafeSingleton with Two Threads)

participant "Thread t1" as T1
participant "ThreadSafeSingleton" as Singleton
participant "Thread t2" as T2

note over Singleton
  instance = null (initially)
  volatile ensures visibility
end note

== Both threads call getInstance() concurrently ==

T1 -> Singleton : getInstance("Thread-1")
activate Singleton #LightBlue

T2 -> Singleton : getInstance("Thread-2")
activate Singleton #LightGreen

note over Singleton
  **First check (no lock)**
  result = instance  // null
end note

T1 -> Singleton : result = instance
note right : result == null

T2 -> Singleton : result = instance
note left : result == null

== Thread t1 acquires lock first ==

T1 -> Singleton : synchronized(ThreadSafeSingleton.class)
activate Singleton #Yellow
note right of Singleton
  **Second check (inside lock)**
  if (instance == null)  // still null
end note

T1 -> Singleton : instance = new ThreadSafeSingleton("Thread-1")
note right : Constructor runs:\nthis.data = "Thread-1"\nThread.sleep(1000)

Singleton --> T1 : instance (data="Thread-1")
deactivate Singleton

note over Singleton
  instance is now set
  (volatile write visible to all threads)
end note

== Thread t2 acquires lock ==

T2 -> Singleton : synchronized(ThreadSafeSingleton.class)
activate Singleton #Yellow
note left of Singleton
  **Second check (inside lock)**
  if (instance == null)  // false!
  Instance already created by t1
end note

Singleton --> T2 : instance (data="Thread-1")
deactivate Singleton

note over Singleton
  Both threads receive the
  **same instance** with
  data = "Thread-1"
end note

deactivate Singleton
deactivate Singleton

T1 -> T1 : println("T1 data: " + s.getData())
note right : Output: "T1 data: Thread-1"

T2 -> T2 : println("T2 data: " + s.getData())
note left : Output: "T2 data: Thread-1"

note over T1, T2
  **Result:** Only ONE instance created.
  Both threads share the same ThreadSafeSingleton.
end note

@enduml
